Solution: Using a Linux terminal, SSH into the machine. The command structure of SSH is ssh <username>@<server> -p <port>
Username should be the username mentioned, server should be a valid URL or a correct IP address, and -p <port> won't be necessary if we connect to port 22 (standard port).

ssh bandit0@bandit.labs.overthewire.org -p 2220
password: bandit0 (already given)

By now, you should be logged into the machine.
